research_rationale:
EO 13326 established the President's Commission on Implementation of United States Space Exploration Policy and contains no provision other than those of a commission order (membership, mission, administration, reports, termination). Its termination clause reads "(b) The Commission shall terminate within 60 days after submitting its final report." That clause is triggered by the date of a report and is not an end under owner ruling 2026-10-21-report-deadline; the report date is not held in any source in the repository, so it is disclosed here and not recorded as an end. Section 3 of EO 13385 of September 29, 2005 (70 FR 57989, published October 4, 2005)  revokes the order by number with the words "(b) Executive Order 13326, establishing the President ’s Commission on 
Implementation of United States Space Exploration Policy." and the first dated end held is 2005-09-30. 
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Own text: the order's termination clause (\"(b) The Commission shall terminate within 60 days after submitting its \nfinal report.\") depends on the date of a final report that no held source dates; under the report-deadline ruling it is disclosed and not treated as an end. No fixed calendar sunset appears in the order. Searched held texts by the order's number: only the order's own copies and the revoking order cite it. No earlier revocation or supersession is held.","independent_command_check":"All commands in the order establish, staff, direct or report from the commission; none is an independent continuing command outside it. The revocation is express and unqualified, so no clause is carved out.","savings_check":"No savings language appears in the revoking order for EO 13326.","scope_check":"The inventory is the 20 scopes the packet derives from the Federal Register text of EO 13326; every scope belongs to the single commission order, and Section 3 of EO 13385 of September 29, 2005 (70 FR 57989, published October 4, 2005) revokes the order as a whole without exception."}

EO 13762 of January 13, 2017 (82 FR 7619) set an order of succession for the office of Attorney General (section 1), exceptions (section 2), revoked EO 13557 (section 3) and added a no-rights provision (section 4). EO 13775 of February 9, 2017 (82 FR 10697) enacted a replacement succession list and in its section 3 states: "Executive Order 13762 of January 
13, 2017, is revoked." Section 1 of EO 13762 runs only until at least one named senior officer can act, a standing contingency that does not end the order. The held corpus holds no earlier revocation or amendment of EO 13762; the first end of the order as a whole is February 9, 2017, although its section 3 clause was performed earlier, on issuance (2017-01-13). Section 3 of EO 13762 ("Executive Order 13557 of November 4, 2010, is revoked.") is a self-executing revocation performed when the order issued on 2017-01-13, so its clause has an earlier first end by performance; the other clauses end with the revocation of the order by EO 13775 on 2017-02-09 (EO 13775 has no effective-date section, so the revocation took effect on signing). A by-number search of the held order texts for EO 13762 finds this order's own text and EO 13775 (Federal Register and American Presidency Project copies), and no other instrument.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Own terms: section 1 operates only during a vacancy and 'until such time as at least one of the officers mentioned above is able to perform the functions and duties of that office', a recurring contingency, not a sunset. Searched held texts by the order's number: only EO 13775 and the order's own copies cite it. No earlier revocation, supersession or amendment is held.","independent_command_check":"Section 3 of EO 13762 (revocation of EO 13557) is a one-time self-executing command, performed on issuance, and has its own earlier first end; section 4 is a no-rights statement that ends with the order. Neither is an independent continuing command that outlived the revocation.","savings_check":"The surviving consequence is the revocation of EO 13557; EO 13775 does not reinstate it. The order of succession itself is replaced by EO 13775.","scope_check":"Inventory is 10 scopes (a lead paragraph, sections 1 to 4 and their subsections) taken from 82 FR 7619-7620. EO 13775 section 3 revokes the whole order, so every scope ends on the same date."}

